## Why This Is Asked
This question tests the ability to design a low-level concurrent router with per-producer ordering, a bounded queue, and a controlled degradation path using sampling. It demonstrates practical handling of backpressure and fairness without requiring large-scale infrastructure.

## Key Concepts
- **Per-agent FIFO buffers** preserve ordering for each producer
- **Global bounded queue** with backpressure signaling to prevent memory exhaustion
- **Sampling mode** to throttle backlog growth when system is overwhelmed
- **Fairness**: round-robin or alternating drain across agents
- **Graceful degradation and shutdown**: handling backlog when load normalizes and safely draining on shutdown

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simplified architecture:
// 1. Each agent has a dedicated FIFO buffer
// 2. Global dispatcher reads from buffers in round-robin fashion
// 3. When total backlog exceeds THRESHOLD, enable sampling mode

class EventRouter {
  constructor(workerCount, samplingThreshold, sampleRate) {
    this.agents = new Map();
    this.globalQueue = new BoundedQueue(1000);
    this.workers = new WorkerPool(workerCount);
    this.samplingThreshold = samplingThreshold;
    this.sampleRate = sampleRate; // K
    this.samplingMode = false;
  }

  registerAgent(agentId) {
    this.agents.set(agentId, { buffer: [], paused: false });
  }

  async submit(agentId, event) {
    const agent = this.agents.get(agentId);
    if (!agent) throw new Error(`Unknown agent: ${agentId}`);

    const totalBacklog = this.calculateBacklog();

    if (totalBacklog > this.samplingThreshold && !this.samplingMode) {
      this.samplingMode = true;
    }

    if (this.samplingMode) {
      if (this.sampleCounter++ % this.sampleRate === 0) {
        await this.globalQueue.offer(event);
      } else {
        agent.buffer.push(event);
      }
    } else {
      agent.buffer.push(event);
    }
  }

  calculateBacklog() {
    return Array.from(this.agents.values())
      .reduce((sum, a) => sum + a.buffer.length, 0);
  }

  // Graceful fallback: resume queued events when backlog recedes
  maybeExitSamplingMode() {
    if (this.samplingMode && this.calculateBacklog() < this.samplingThreshold * 0.5) {
      this.samplingMode = false;
      this.drainQueuedEvents();
    }
  }
}
```

## Test Plan

### 1. Per-Agent Ordering Test
- Register 3 agents (A, B, C)
- Submit events in order: A1, A2, A3, B1, B2, B3, C1, C2, C3
- Verify output preserves per-agent sequence: A events arrive in order, same for B and C
- Run 1000 iterations with different submission patterns

### 2. Sampling Accuracy Test
- Set sampleRate = 10 (forward every 10th event)
- Submit 1000 events from a single agent
- Verify ~100 events forwarded immediately, ~900 queued
- Confirm queued events are forwarded after sampling mode exits

### 3. Backpressure Test
- Fill buffers to capacity
- Verify submit() blocks or rejects when queue is full
- Verify memory stays bounded under load

### 4. Fairness Test
- Submit 1000 events each from 5 agents
- Verify no agent is starved (each gets processed)
- Measure inter-arrival times between agents

### 5. Shutdown Test
- Start router with pending events in buffers
- Initiate graceful shutdown
- Verify all in-flight events complete
- Verify no events are lost

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests real-world concurrency understanding: preserving per-region ordering under backpressure, implementing fairness across regions, and enabling dynamic worker resizing without breaking guarantees.

## Key Concepts

- **Per-region ordering**: Monotonic counters ensure events within each region maintain FIFO order across all pipeline stages
- **Bounded queues and backpressure**: Backpressure signaling prevents memory exhaustion when producers outpace consumers
- **Regional fairness scheduler**: Weighted round-robin allocates processing slots proportionally to region weights
- **Dynamic worker resizing**: Per-region worker pools can scale independently without violating ordering guarantees
- **Late/out-of-order event handling**: Watermark-based windowing and retries for events arriving after their expected timestamp

## Code Example

```javascript
class RegionBuffer {
  constructor(limit) {
    this.queue = [];
    this.limit = limit;
    this.nextSeq = 0;
  }

  enqueue(event) {
    if (this.queue.length >= this.limit) {
      throw new BackpressureError('region buffer full');
    }
    event.seq = this.nextSeq++;
    this.queue.push(event);
    return event;
  }

  dequeue() {
    return this.queue.shift();
  }

  isFull() {
    return this.queue.length >= this.limit;
  }
}

class RegionalFairnessScheduler {
  constructor(regions, weights) {
    this.regionBuffers = new Map();
    this.weights = weights;
    this.counters = new Map();
    this.currentIndex = 0;

    regions.forEach(region => {
      this.regionBuffers.set(region, new RegionBuffer(1000));
      this.counters.set(region, 0);
    });
  }

  schedule() {
    const regions = Array.from(this.regionBuffers.keys());
    const weight = this.weights[regions[this.currentIndex]] || 1;

    if (this.counters.get(regions[this.currentIndex]) < weight) {
      const buffer = this.regionBuffers.get(regions[this.currentIndex]);
      if (buffer.queue.length > 0) {
        this.counters.set(regions[this.currentIndex], 
          this.counters.get(regions[this.currentIndex]) + 1);
        return buffer.dequeue();
      }
    }

    this.currentIndex = (this.currentIndex + 1) % regions.length;
    if (this.counters.get(regions[this.currentIndex]) >= weight) {
      this.counters.set(regions[this.currentIndex], 0);
    }
    return null;
  }
}
```

## Test Plan

### 1. Burst Handling Test
- Send 10x normal load from a single region
- Verify other regions still receive processing slots
- Confirm no starvation occurs

### 2. Late Events Test
- Introduce events with out-of-sequence timestamps
- Configure late-tolerance window (e.g., 5 seconds)
- Verify late events are handled according to policy (drop/retry/reject)

### 3. Backpressure Test
- Fill regional buffers to capacity
- Verify backpressure signal is emitted to producers
- Confirm producers throttle correctly
- Test backpressure release when buffer drains

### 4. Dynamic Worker Resizing Test
- Increase worker count mid-operation for a region
- Verify ordering maintained through the transition
- Decrease workers and confirm graceful degradation

### 5. Recovery Test
- Simulate region failure and recovery
- Confirm ordering guarantees restore after recovery

